go here. The user is asking for actual data from the GitHub API, so I likely need to read up on the GitHub skill. It looks like there’s one specific skill that applies, which is the GitHub skill. I'll check that out to get started!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_SZtQwsNNE8SCWnY9nF7sL7y1|fc_079497c67bfb17b50169b5f68d889c8191aa00a464bb3f2d68","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/github/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/github/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":14895,"output":83,"cacheRead":2560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17538,"cost":{"input":0.0372375,"output":0.001245,"cacheRead":0.0006399999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.039122500000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773532807247}}
{"type":"message","id":"c1027545","parentId":"17afb3a2","timestamp":"2026-03-15T00:00:12.114Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_SZtQwsNNE8SCWnY9nF7sL7y1|fc_079497c67bfb17b50169b5f68d889c8191aa00a464bb3f2d68","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: github\ndescription: \"Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\"\n---\n\n# GitHub Skill\n\nUse the `gh` CLI to interact with GitHub. Always specify `--repo owner/repo` when not in a git directory, or use URLs directly.\n\n## Pull Requests\n\nCheck CI status on a PR:\n```bash\ngh pr checks 55 --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nList recent workflow runs:\n```bash\ngh run list --repo owner/repo --limit 10\n```\n\nView a run and see which steps failed:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nView logs for failed steps only:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo --log-failed\n```\n\n## API for Advanced Queries\n\nThe `gh api` command is useful for accessing data not available through other subcommands.\n\nGet PR with specific fields:\n```bash\ngh api repos/owner/repo/pulls/55 --jq '.title, .state, .user.login'\n```\n\n## JSON Output\n\nMost commands support `--json` for structured output.  You can use `--jq` to filter:\n\n```bash\ngh issue list --repo owner/repo --json number,title --jq '.[] | \"\\(.number): \\(.title)\"'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773532812113}}
{"type":"message","id":"6381db82","parentId":"c1027545","timestamp":"2026-03-15T00:00:24.921Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Fetching repository data**\n\nI need to fetch data and I could use an exec command with the GitHub API and probably jq. First, I need the current date to search for repositories based on their creation date and stars. I want to find the top 5 repositories with archived set to false and sort them by descending stars. Maybe I should consider adding a filter for pushed activity in the last 90 days. I’ll also need to deduplicate across sections and keep the response concise!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_079497c67bfb17b50169b5f69439e881919a1788fa1a0c6be2\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptfaX15SZTHVAEFzfonan-fLz0gZNwop5gczX8N8l8PaeTpc_X0dlLFXEjAO_VAyr_QfFvX9U-wM_a953UeEw_zOhsrc4w85yHyvzrqcAsfMwdJom8W07RyhOKXpKXl4GvwYkfwn7l1GGq9pp1_q2oO5PrfMQT61L_6RnFHopRRUNdXTgLz2ViP8Kwe23SOx3cTxVi_h513wde7OYzlN-IARHGeUcULSZ2lIWbBq4wgOsd2qIHgDK4ojzrzMWh2nDgquBovA0U6pMVOpdbZgR3Fj4pa3cLNPDLGHs4afITzOlaIlGEybFgSh2iNxZJ2UbEO5xClXwbQFURSX9mQSsuWSDz2ww3n-5KsfG7dP2Gzgzm-D3skFmaoA9x6RcIOpuuvoT7Vo_9vE_j9w9kKuI6xnxItADf-rKIpaFGuEeud6OV4fNaMsMQsA5z4LbXooKhsuGut6S4OKpWxJQW2ombXbOjTpNnr_sbQo-omvjnjzsZzocC7AaVu_MPj5His58_yJF0jiYQ2r8S-sAafIXI_uH0QSrYzBEOr_RN6wt9VS0XUX-jM66_DQL-Xcj7YRSXoDhYcC4UIJTm-ntbf_ga6F3SkEdfTupg43pfy0gS6qGVZ-oShP1w94QNmGmK3JR4mrzaAhfvp9DJaFCipfgHaRFX_YUBGKiZWmwnpQjIl9KLcGwOc1fMzQVaDZrpPsA7AsExmecjjjdDg5c8mUTv2eqYCKCFYgx933GnOPwRRiVO3DniNwT4QhQev2VRWyAZgbqFaVodGG-LDYzsj2k13unph2Py0PscOGPbpLDwGjlq9RUBVmoWF8b8lpHhHttrwXGjBZLXbYtA7yekU-zwAQXBkpNn3ptpXl2JPAnwcNncjHQ2dYorDJZWL8DM94mqNgCwbEU1ZPW6vtCxKQxFvF4zBnQM8EKnQPNX_09N7rfHeYcpa3tv8_ReVVdAWv80pmH09vwgdhfdshf3PzpdNDiRqI7Zz3r9FXX-Xopvyhv7UwjQk6B93PHl299C08GWByDw_w6DlhOykvXtb5--owtzFvjjtHAbtfrxfPc-rRu4PPr658Ab98C6JQHWVINGW_ZlMJHo5cwhHLiitEUsd8SVJpqhY2R2JvefBw3a2Rr5HtW88gwSkNAg0ZqZ-0ZgQQg7cOHUhDkCBFGm-1gAGKoqfkvD9Q7jLXQpqSQEKeoz_M3dzffv_ml6xZTel2xhz-Vz2DpdUcpq6B3CzE5f3IBzwPJR5vle2HH601nnUGwne0WAXq0_DLGM4kFeXBMtk0U2uThVAqnK05olUKqHWHDxCJsSVR9cfT2ZDm154HYcLkdDTZjzS9BhjY0XcnVFg98\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Fetching repository data**\\n\\nI need to fetch data and I could use an exec command with the GitHub API and probably jq. First, I need the current date to search for repositories based on their creation date and stars. I want to find the top 5 repositories with archived set to false and sort them by descending stars. Maybe I should consider adding a filter for pushed activity in the last 90 days. I’ll also need to deduplicate across sections and keep the response concise!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_I2tyXXDn5pHHlyfB0QCh3NZD|fc_079497c67bfb17b50169b5f69799608191b55abb7219b26066","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport datetime, subprocess, json, textwrap\nnow = datetime.datetime(2026,3,15,0,0,0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\nsince = (now - datetime.timedelta(days=7)).date().isoformat()\nqueries = {\n  'recent': f'search/repositories?q=created:>={since}+stars:>1+archived:false&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=10',\n  'alltime': 'search/repositories?q=stars:>50000+archived:false+pushed:>=2025-09-01&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=10'\n}\nfor k,q in queries.items():\n    out = subprocess.check_output(['gh','api',q], text=True)\n    data = json.loads(out)\n    print('###', k)\n    for i,item in enumerate(data['items'][:10],1):\n        print(json.dumps({\n            'rank': i,\n            'full_name': item['full_name'],\n            'stars': item['stargazers_count'],\n            'created_at': item['created_at'],\n            'pushed_at': item['pushed_at'],\n            'desc': item.get('description'),\n            'lang': item.get('language'),\n            'url': item['html_url']\n        }, ensure_ascii=False))\nPY"},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nimport datetime, subprocess, json, textwrap\\nnow = datetime.datetime(2026,3,15,0,0,0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\\nsince = (now - datetime.timedelta(days=7)).date().isoformat()\\nqueries = {\\n  'recent': f'search/repositories?q=created:>={since}+stars:>1+archived:false&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=10',\\n  'alltime': 'search/repositories?q=stars:>50000+archived:false+pushed:>=2025-09-01&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=10'\\n}\\nfor k,q in queries.items():\\n    out = subprocess.check_output(['gh','api',q], text=True)\\n    data = json.loads(out)\\n    print('###', k)\\n    for i,item in enumerate(data['items'][:10],1):\\n        print(json.dumps({\\n            'rank': i,\\n            'full_name': item['full_name'],\\n            'stars': item['stargazers_count'],\\n            'created_at': item['created_at'],\\n            'pushed_at': item['pushed_at'],\\n            'desc': item.get('description'),\\n            'lang': item.get('language'),\\n            'url': item['html_url']\\n        }, ensure_ascii=False))\\nPY\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":450,"output":425,"cacheRead":17408,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18283,"cost":{"input":0.0011250000000000001,"output":0.0063750000000000005,"cacheRead":0.004352,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011852000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773532812115}}
